title: acheshkov/program_slicing (Python Library)
authors: acheshkov (GitHub)
year: 2021-2022 (approximate)
venue: GitHub
quality: CODE
url: https://github.com/acheshkov/program_slicing
keywords: Python, Java, PDG, CFG, CDG, DDG, program slicing, tree-sitter, networkx, extract method
content:
  LANGUAGE: Python 57%, Java support as analysis target
  IMPLEMENTS: Tsantalis/Chatzigeorgiou (2011) complete computation slice algorithm
  
  GRAPH STRUCTURES (all inherit networkx.DiGraph):
    - CFG (Control Flow Graph): execution paths
    - CDG (Control Dependence Graph): control dependencies
    - DDG (Data Dependence Graph): variable dependencies
    - PDG (Program Dependence Graph): combined CDG + DDG
  
  STATEMENT TYPES: FUNCTION, VARIABLE, ASSIGNMENT, CALL, SCOPE, BRANCH, LOOP, GOTO, UNKNOWN, EXIT
  
  STATEMENT PROPERTIES:
    - statement_type (enum)
    - start_point, end_point (position)
    - affected_by (variable dependencies)
    - name, ast_node_type
  
  MANAGER CLASS: ProgramGraphsManager
    Methods: extracting dominated/reachable blocks, identifying affected statements,
    detecting redundant constructs, retrieving statements in scopes/ranges.
  
  CLI: 'slice' command -- decomposes source files into slices
  
  AST PARSING: tree-sitter
  GRAPH OPS: NetworkX
  REQUIRES: Python 3.9+, C compiler
  
  NOTE: No standalone cohesion metrics computation; focused on slice extraction for
  refactoring identification.
<<<END>>>

