id: 36
ts: 2026-05-29T10:46:00Z
relevance: MED
title: Ottenstein/Ottenstein 1984: Program Dependence Graph in Software Development Environment
authors: Karl J. Ottenstein, Linda M. Ottenstein
year: 1984
venue: Proceedings ACM SIGSOFT/SIGPLAN Software Engineering Symposium on Practical Software Development Environments, pp. 177-184
quality: PEER-REVIEWED
url: https://digitalcommons.mtu.edu/michigantech-p/12603/
keywords: PDG, program dependence graph, slicing, vertex reachability, linear time
content:
  FIRST PAPER to connect PDGs to slicing.
  
  KEY OBSERVATION: Given a program represented as a PDG, the slicing problem reduces to
  a vertex-reachability problem. Thus slices can be computed in LINEAR TIME O(V+E).
  
  This is the insight that makes PDG-based slicing practical. Before this, Weiser's
  original slicing algorithm required multiple dataflow passes (more expensive).
  
  Preceded Ferrante/Ottenstein/Warren 1987 (which formalized the PDG definition more fully)
  and Horwitz/Reps/Binkley 1990 (which extended to interprocedural SDG).
<<<END>>>


